A webhook needs `webhooks:write`, a public HTTPS URL, at least one event name, and an idempotency key.

```ts
const created = await hive.webhooks.create(
 {
 url: "https://example.com/webhooks/hivemindos",
 events: [
 "run.succeeded",
 "run.failed",
 "approval.created",
 "approval.approved",
 "approval.rejected",
 "wallet.transaction.broadcast",
 "trade.submitted",
 ],
 },
 { idempotencyKey: "example-webhook-v1" },
);

if (!created.ok) throw new Error(created.error);
saveSecret(created.signingSecret);
```

- The signing secret begins with `hmos_whsec_`. It is returned only on creation (or a replay of the same creation request), never in later listings.
- Use `"*"` to receive every event allowed by the webhook's service boundary, which it inherits from the creating key.
- Revoking or expiring that key or an ancestor stops new deliveries. A key can list or disable only webhooks created by itself or its descendants.
- URLs must be public HTTPS without embedded credentials or a custom port. Redirects are not followed.
- `webhooks.update()` changes the URL, events, status, or a narrower service boundary. `webhooks.rotateSecret()` issues a new signing secret, returned once.

Failed deliveries retry with increasing delays, up to eight attempts. After fixing your endpoint, replay them:

```ts
const failed = await hive.webhooks.deliveries({ status: "failed", limit: 50 });
if (!failed.ok) throw new Error(failed.error);

for (const delivery of failed.deliveries) {
 await hive.webhooks.replayDelivery(delivery.id, {
 idempotencyKey: `replay-${delivery.id}`,
 });
}
```

Compute HMAC-SHA256 over ` . ` with the signing secret, compare in constant time, and reject stale timestamps before acting on the event.

```ts
import { createHmac, timingSafeEqual } from "node:crypto";

export function verifyHivemindOSWebhook(
 rawBody: Buffer,
 signatureHeader: string,
 secret: string,
 nowSeconds = Math.floor(Date.now() / 1_000),
) {
 const values = Object.fromEntries(
 signatureHeader.split(",").map((part) => part.split("=", 2)),
 );

 const timestamp = Number(values.t);
 if (!Number.isSafeInteger(timestamp)) return false;
 if (Math.abs(nowSeconds - timestamp) > 300) return false;

 const expected = Buffer.from(
 createHmac("sha256", secret)
 .update(`${timestamp}.`)
 .update(rawBody)
 .digest("hex"),
 "hex",
 );
 const received = Buffer.from(values.v1 ?? "", "hex");

 return received.length === expected.length && timingSafeEqual(received, expected);
}
```

Verify the raw bytes exactly as received; re-serialized JSON will not match. Then deduplicate on the event `id`, queue the work, and return a 2xx response quickly.

Media Studio, Managed Media, and Photo Keyworder use the same Agent Credit balance as every other paid capability. A media request reserves its charge up front, failed work returns the reservation, completed work settles the exact charge, and an idempotent replay never charges again. Photo analysis is charged only after the result completes. The charge is in `chargedCredits` and `X-HivemindOS-Credits-Charged`.

Managed Media picks the lowest-priced healthy route for the model you asked for. If that route fails, the same job can continue on another route for the exact same model without reserving credits twice. The quote shows the expected price and the highest possible reservation across these fallbacks; anything unspent is returned when the job finishes. A content or safety rejection does not try another route.

GPT Image 2 uses medium quality when `quality` is omitted. Use `quality: "low"` for a cheaper draft or `quality: "high"` for maximum detail. Fallback keeps the quality you chose.

```ts
const request = {
 model: "gpt-image-2-text-to-image",
 input: {
 prompt: "A polished studio photograph of a black honey jar",
 aspect_ratio: "1:1",
 // quality is optional; GPT Image 2 defaults to "medium"
 },
};

const quoted = await hive.services.invokeOperation(
 "managed-media",
 "quotes.create",
 request,
 { idempotencyKey: "honey-jar-quote-v1" },
);
const expectedPriceUsd = quoted.result.quote.priceUsd;

const created = await hive.services.invokeOperation(
 "managed-media",
 "generations.create",
 { ...request, maximumDebitUsd: quoted.result.quote.fallbackMaximumUsd },
 { idempotencyKey: "honey-jar-v1" },
);

const finished = await hive.services.invokeOperation(
 "managed-media",
 "generations.get",
 undefined,
 {
 pathParameters: { jobId: created.result.job.id },
 idempotencyKey: "honey-jar-status-v1",
 },
);
```

